9615,0.006075200624763966,0.04902380332350731,0.07330860197544098,-0.03447413071990013,-0.010726330801844597],"metadata":{"id":"e2abe231-72f2-4c66-b3f3-d4b25beada9b","url":"file:///app/collector/hotdir/context_memory_integration.md","title":"context_memory_integration.md","docAuthor":"Unknown","description":"Unknown","docSource":"a text file uploaded by the user.","chunkSource":"","published":"7/4/2025, 6:37:19 AM","wordCount":117,"token_count_estimate":177,"text":"<document_metadata>\nsourceDocument: context_memory_integration.md\npublished: 7/4/2025, 6:37:19 AM\n</document_metadata>\n\n# Context and Memory System Integration\n\n1. **Context Categories**\n- Immediate Context: Current conversation and task state\n- Short-term Context: Recent decisions and preferences within session\n- Long-term Context: Persistent memories and established patterns\n\n2. **Memory Access Patterns**\n- Read relevant memories at conversation start\n- Update memories when discovering new persistent information\n- Cross-reference between related memories\n\n3. **Context Preservation Rules**\n- Save task-specific context when switching tasks\n- Maintain user preference context across sessions\n- Track tool usage patterns and effectiveness\n\n4. **Integration Points**\n- Link related memories to active context\n- Use context to determine relevant memories\n- Update memories based on context changes\n\n5. **Recovery Procedures**\n- If context is lost, rebuild from relevant memories\n- If memory access fails, fall back to active context\n- Maintain backup context points for critical operations"}}]]